
  SIGMA(n) = 2n + PHI(n): THE UNIQUENESS OF 42

======================================================================

  I. THE IDENTITY
  --------------------------------------------------

  sigma(42) = 96
  phi(42)   = 12
  2 * 42    = 84
  sigma(42) - 2*42 = 12 = phi(42)? True

  II. EXHAUSTIVE SEARCH: n = 1 to 100000
  --------------------------------------------------

  Solutions to sigma(n) = 2n + phi(n) for n <= 100000:
    n = 12: sigma=28, 2n=24, phi=4, sigma-2n-phi = 0
    n = 42: sigma=96, 2n=84, phi=12, sigma-2n-phi = 0
    n = 1242: sigma=2880, 2n=2484, phi=396, sigma-2n-phi = 0

  Solutions: [12, 42, 1242]

  Near misses (|sigma - 2n - phi| <= 5, first 20):
